Third-party components
----------------------

None. Nearby has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on 26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the room export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

The transport gap
-----------------

A LAN transport does exist in this estate — `lan-kit`, zero dependencies, SSE and POST — but it is not wired into this app. What ships here is a same-device bus, so the room logic runs and can be tested. The engine takes a bus with send/on and ships with a same-device bus, so
the proximity logic runs and can be tested. A real peer link over the venue network would be a runtime
network call, which this fleet does not make, and faking it would misrepresent the one thing this app
exists to do.

What the app does do — the venue graph, the three tiers, the meet-point pins, the board — is real logic,
tested, with no coordinates anywhere.

Privacy
-------

There is no latitude, longitude, distance in metres, bearing or radius in this app. Proximity is a hop
count between named anchors, reduced to one of three words, and the hop count is not shown to the user.
A check-in replaces the previous one, so there is no trail.
